  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8909a7b854c460945b7273a620ed017e, type: 3}
  m_Name: PoI_01_Susan
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  speakerName: Storyteller
  characterAvatar: {fileID: 0}
  arrivalPrompt: You have arrived at the site.
  arrivalButtonText: Start
  dialogueLines:
  - "My name is Susan. I grew up here in Christchurch, and it\u2019s still my home
    today."
  - Standing here in Cathedral Square now, it feels quite different from what I remember.
    The tower and spire are missing, but they hold a special place in my memory.
    You used to be able to see it from almost anywhere in the city.
  - "Back in high school, I got lost around Cathedral Square during a field trip.
    I remembered my teacher, Mr Watson, always told us: 'If you are lost, look for
    the Cathedral spire\u2014it's the tallest building in the town!' I heard the
    bell, looked up, and found my way back."
  - The last time I saw the Cathedral standing as it once was was right before the
    earthquake, when I visited the Square with my homestay student, Wen. We had no
    idea how much that ordinary afternoon would come to mean to us.
  - "Now, when I pass by here, I still see the absence of that spire. I always try
    to look up as I used to, and outline its contours in my mind \u2014 it's a habit
    that never left me."
  - Even when you weren't standing right next to it, knowing where the Cathedral
    was helped you find your bearings. I suppose it was always a part of how I knew
    I was home..
  alignmentPrompt: Position yourself to match the historical perspective.
  alignmentButtonText: I'm in Position
  interactionInstruction: 
  interactionButtonText: Got it
  reflectionPrompt: 'Take a moment to reflect on what you''ve just experienced: What
    did the Cathedral mean to the people living in this city?'
  reflectionButtonText: Continue
